301
      Figure 3 shows the pattern in individual images. On a chest radiograph, the Effusion and Nodule
302   writes raise the same answers. The competing write raises the Effusion answer more than the Effusion
303   write does. On a natural image, the dog write moves only the dog answer. The write matrix reveals
304   two components of the deficit (Figure 4, Table 11). First, concept writes in the chest datasets have
305   little effect on their own answers. The median 𝑊𝑞,𝑞 is 0.011 on NIH and 0.021 on CheXpert,
306   compared with 0.238 on COCO. Writes meet the steering reference—beating the random family and
307   the sham—in 44 of 246 chest cells, versus 103 of 120 COCO cells. Second, when a chest write moves
308   an answer, competing directions share its effect. Of those 44 cells, 8 have a stronger competitor and 7
309   are unresolved (Table 10). Across the grid, the Atelectasis, Effusion, and Consolidation directions
310
      raise each other’s answers by similar amounts. On COCO, the diagonal entry of 𝑊 dominates its
      row. On NIH and CheXpert, the row is flat or peaks off the diagonal. At every Qwen2.5-VL size, a
311
      competing direction—Cardiomegaly at 3B, Nodule at 7B and 32B, Atelectasis at 72B—raises the
312
      Effusion answer more than the Effusion direction does.
313
314
315
      5.2     The seed finding replicates on new patients
316
      The evaluation builds on a two-model NIH study of Qwen2.5-VL-7B and LLaVA-1.5-7B (Appendix B).
317
      We reproduce the central result in a 600-image cohort disjoint from every earlier cohort (Table 27).
318   The Effusion write raises the Effusion answer by 0.190. This effect exceeds the random 95th
319   percentile (0.137) and sham (0.017). It ranks second among the 120 compared effects. Yet the Nodule
320   direction raises the Effusion answer by 0.262. Effusion ownership is 𝑂 Effusion = −0.071 (95% CI
321   [−0.080, −0.062]), matching the original −0.057 [−0.069, −0.045]. Prompt dependence for Mass
322   also reproduces. Effusion and Cardiomegaly are the most readable chest concepts (mean selectivity
323   0.17 and 0.19 over 41 chest blocks). Effusion is owned in 6 of 41 chest blocks. Among these owned
      blocks, 5 have 𝑂 Effusion ≤ 0.03.


