354   5.3                                              The write mechanism is intact on natural objects
355
356
      The same procedure yields the opposite result on COCO (Table 1, right block). Objects are owned
      in 101 of 120 cells (84%), with ownership margins of 0.1–0.9 in the Qwen, Lingshu, and Gemma
357
      families. 103 cells meet the steering reference. Only 10 cells have a stronger competitor. Among the
358
      20 checkpoints with a COCO block, 17 own at least four of the six objects. Dose response tracks
359   the write. On COCO, median ownership across questions and blocks rises from −0.03 at 𝛼 = −0.1
360   to +0.26 at 𝛼 = +0.25 and remains positive at 𝛼 = +0.5 (+0.18). On NIH, median ownership
361   stays within ±0.1 at every dose (Figure 2c). The write, direction construction, reference family, and
362   decision rules therefore work as intended. The deficit is specific to clinical concepts.
363
364   5.4                                              Ownership belongs to the reader
365
366   Gemma 3 shares one SigLIP tower across its 4B, 12B, and 27B checkpoints. MedGemma shares
367   one MedSigLIP tower across 4B and 27B. LLaVA-1.5 shares one CLIP tower across 7B and 13B.
368   We intervene primarily at the tower’s final block. Within each family, pooled features, fitted probes,
369
      and write vectors are therefore identical across sizes (bit-identical for Gemma 3 4B and 12B and
      for LLaVA-1.5; equal within one bf16 rounding step for Gemma 3 27B and MedGemma 27B,
370
      direction cosines above 0.9987). Readability is identical across sizes by construction. The connector
371
      and language model determine every difference in Figure 5 by how they read the same written
372   representation. The median paired difference is 0.6–3.7 times the refit standard deviation. It exceeds
373   that standard deviation in 7 of the 8 pairs with a refit estimate (Table 15). With the identical write
374   on the same 600 patients, Gemma 3 4B and 12B differ in 𝑂 𝑞 by −0.83 [−0.85, −0.81] on NIH
375   Effusion. The difference between 12B and 27B is +0.79 [+0.76, +0.82]. In 11 of the 12 shared-tower
376   pair–dataset combinations, the paired patient-bootstrap interval for Δ𝑂 𝑞 excludes zero for five or
377   six of the six concepts. The median |Δ𝑂 𝑞 | is 0.6–3.7 times the families’ refit standard deviation
      (up to 8.8 times for single concepts). In 12B, competing directions own the chest answers outright


