415   5.5    Size and family
416
      On the chest sets, ownership is concentrated among a few readers and varies by concept and dataset
417
      (Figure 6; Table 4). Qwen2.5-VL owns no concepts at 3B or 7B. It owns Cardiomegaly at 32B. At
418
      72B, it owns Atelectasis (𝑂 = 0.54), Cardiomegaly, and Mass. Effusion is anti-owned at every size.
419   Lingshu, the medical Qwen2.5-VL derivative, owns three CheXpert concepts at 7B and five at 32B,
420   the highest clinical ownership in the grid. InternVL3.5 answers every NIH question at every size. Its
421   writes on the chest sets remain within 0.04 of zero. LLaVA-1.5 reads the chest concepts but answers
422   none above chance. It owns none.
423
424   5.6    Controls and alternatives
425
426   Across the grid, the reference family and additional controls behave as designed (Figure 2d; Table 11).
427   Owned concept writes rank 1–6 among the 120 compared effects. On the chest sets, the concept write
428   typically ranks in the top decile.
429
430   Geometry, scale, saturation, refits, numerics. No measurement alternative explains the deficit
431   (Tables 12–24; Appendix A.7). The strongest competitor matches the most similar direction or the
      most co-occurring label at chance rate. Logit-scale verdicts agree in 358 of 366 cells. COCO blocks


