648
      A     Campaign details
649
650
      This appendix lists the checkpoints and their consumed loci, the acceptance decisions, the coverage of
651
      the campaign, and the per-concept results of every completed block.
652
653
      A.1   Labels, registration, and artifact
654
655
      Labels. Concept labels are the report-derived labels supplied with each dataset (NIH ChestX-
656   ray14 finding labels; the CheXpert labeler output distributed with CheXpert Plus; COCO instance
657   annotations). A row is positive for label 1, negative for label 0, and unknown for uncertain or blank
658   labeler outputs. We exclude unknown rows from probe fitting, selectivity, and answer AUROC. We
659   write and score these rows like all others. Fixed manifests drawn with recorded seeds define the
660   cohorts. Training and test cohorts are patient-disjoint. All cohorts are disjoint from every seed-study
661   cohort. Table 5 gives per-concept counts. A second CheXpert cohort contains 200 frontal films
662   from the CheXpert validation set, one per patient, with the radiologists’ consensus labels. It has zero
663   patient overlap with every campaign cohort (Table 25).
664
665   Registration. The protocol was frozen before any grid block was scored. The loci, projection and
666   probe settings, dose, reference family, six templates, module set, seven gates, and three decision
667
      rules are those of the registered protocol file and its code commit. The seed study’s crossover and
      confirmation analyses were registered before they were run (Appendix B). One analysis pass over the
668
      packaged outcomes produces everything reported per block. The leaderboard, write-flow share, and
669
      per-image examples are descriptive summaries of these outputs, added after the grid was complete.
670
671
      Artifact. The release contains evaluation code and adapters, the registered protocol file, cohort
672
      manifests with their seeds, fitted directions, per-image outcomes for every module (write, dose, refit,
673   locus, and template rows), every block’s scorecard and coverage file, and rendered prompts. Adding a
674   new checkpoint requires one adapter that names the block it consumes and passes the gates.
675
676
