733
734
735   A.3      Acceptance decisions
736
737   All 61 completed blocks pass checks (A), (B), (C), and (G) with zero determinism error, zero
738   change at 𝛼 = 0, and fp32-versus-model logit differences below 0.13. In check (D), the Qwen3-VL,
739   Gemma 3, MedGemma, InternVL, and Llama families exceed the 0.25-logit tolerance (up to 1.84
740   logits for Gemma 3 12B). We record these as declared deviations and neutralise them through fixed
741   batch composition. Check (E) fails for the A/B templates for LLaVA-1.5-7B and LLaVA-Med,
742   the B-mapped templates for Qwen2.5-VL-3B and LLaVA-1.5-13B, and the yes/no and A-mapped
743   templates for Llama 3.2 Vision 11B on all datasets. We record the affected cells as ineligible. Two
744
      checkpoints answer “yes” to nearly every chest question (Gemma 3 4B: clean 𝑃(yes) > 0.99 on
      94–97% of rows). The answerability grade records this behaviour. Three checkpoints (LLaVA-1.5
745
      7B/13B, LLaVA-Med) answer at chance.
746
747
748   A.4      Coverage and cost
749
750   Twenty checkpoints are complete on all three datasets (Table 6). Coverage includes every module on
751   NIH and COCO—the write matrix, calibration, the five additional templates, the dose sweep, the two
752   refits, and the connector locus—and the write matrix and calibration on CheXpert. Llama 3.2 Vision
753   11B is graded on its eligible B-positive template IB. Qwen2.5-VL-72B is complete on NIH. The 72B
754   COCO/CheXpert blocks and Llama 3.2 Vision 90B were not run (compute budget). InternVL3.5-38B
755   is complete on all three datasets. The campaign consumed about 3,000 A100-hours. A chest block of
      a 7B checkpoint takes about ten GPU-hours.


