992    A.7        Robustness of the deficit
993
994    Each alternative direction is a vector 𝒖 in the projected, train-scaled space. We lift it to the consumed
995    space by normalising ŵ = 𝑅(𝒖 ⊘ max(𝒔, 10−8 )), exactly as for the logistic normal (Equation 2).
996    Here 𝑥 = 𝑅 ⊤ h, where 𝑅 is a fixed Gaussian matrix with near-orthonormal columns. Displacing
997    the consumed representation by 𝑅𝜹 therefore displaces the projected features by 𝑅 ⊤ 𝑅𝜹 ≈ 𝜹. The
998
       same lift applies to classifier normals, class-mean displacements, and patterns. We compute the
       difference-of-means and pattern vectors in the projected space and lift them once. The token-weighted
999
       variants multiply the per-token dose 𝛼∥h𝑖𝑡 ∥ by a weight 𝑤 𝑡 whose mean over the consumed tokens
1000
       is one. The softmax variant preserves the L1 dose of the uniform write. The top-quarter variant
1001   (𝑤 𝑡 = 4 on the 25% highest-scoring tokens) has twice the uniform write’s Frobenius norm. The
1002   attribute directions use three labels from each dataset’s own metadata: the view field (anteroposterior
1003   or portable against posteroanterior), the recorded sex, and age at least 60. We fit these directions
1004   using the same images, features, projection, and probe settings as the clinical probes. We then lift and
1005   write them with the six clinical directions as one nine-direction family. Attribute questions have no
1006   random family, so the sham is their sole steering reference. Their probes reach a median AUROC of
1007   0.896–0.999 against the attribute label and 0.62–0.73 against the model’s own clean answer. The
1008   largest median | cos | between an attribute direction and a clinical normal is 0.10. Across the 30 blocks
1009
       with the module, the attributes are owned in 13 of 90 cells and the findings of the same family in 16
       of 180. The corresponding counts are 5/42 against 10/84 on CheXpert and 8/48 against 6/96 on NIH.
1010
1011
1012   Direction and label geometry. Neither correlations among the six directions nor co-occurrence of
1013   the six report labels explains why a competing direction wins (Table 12). On NIH, the six directions
1014   are as orthogonal as random vectors (mean off-diagonal cosine 0.018 against 0.023 for random pairs).
1015   The labels are nearly uncorrelated (mean 𝜙 = 0.026). Yet NIH shows the same off-diagonal dominance
1016   as CheXpert, where directions and labels are correlated (mean cosine 0.23; Effusion–Consolidation
1017
       0.50, 𝜙 = 0.74). The own direction wins in 25% of NIH and 28% of CheXpert cells. The strongest
       competitor matches the most similar direction at chance rate (19–23%) and the most co-occurring
1018
       label at chance rate (17–23%). Across the 1,230 off-diagonal chest cells, the competitor’s advantage
1019
       𝑊𝑞,𝑑 − 𝑊𝑞,𝑞 is uncorrelated with cosine (Spearman 0.05, 𝑝 = 0.11) and with 𝜙 (0.008). Removing
1020   each cell’s strongest competitor does not restore ownership: 138 of 246 chest cells (56%) have at least
1021   two competitors above the own write. The natural-image families with the highest co-occurrence
1022   (person with bicycle, 𝜙 = 0.14; person with dog; chair with bottle) retain ownership in 95–100% of
1023   cells when competitors are restricted to those families. Of the five directions in the seed cell, Nodule
1024   is the least similar to Effusion (cosine −0.06). It still moves the Effusion answer more than Effusion’s
1025   own direction (0.262 against 0.190). The most similar direction, Atelectasis (cosine 0.49), moves it
       by 0.083.


                                                                                       19
       Under review as a conference paper at ICLR 2027




1026
       Scale, saturation, refits, and numerics. The grades hold on the logit scale. Ownership recomputed
1027   from the margin ℓyes − ℓno agrees with the probability-scale verdict in 358 of 366 cells. Every owned
1028   cell retains 𝑂 𝑞𝑚 > 0, and 127 of 130 retain the full verdict under the same rules (Table 13). Saturation
1029   counters a ceiling explanation: COCO blocks have far more rows at 𝑃(yes) > 0.99 or < 0.01 than
1030   chest blocks (median block share 0.77 against 0.18 and 0.13). Restricting each cell to its unsaturated
1031   rows preserves 𝑂 𝑞 > 0 in all 29 owned chest cells and in 33 of the 207 others. The same pattern holds
1032   in the clean-No, clean-Yes, label-present, and label-absent strata. Refitting the probes on resampled
1033   training patients changes 𝑂 𝑞 by a median of 0.03. The bf16 batch effects declared at the gates
1034   (candidate-logit differences of 0.07–1.84) leave the verdicts unchanged. The margin sign agrees in
1035   55 of 61 blocks; the 6 disagreeing blocks contain no owned cell. Re-scoring the clean baseline in a
1036
       second module gives bitwise agreement in 100% of rows for 36 of 56 blocks and in at least 25% for
       the rest, with |Δ𝑃(yes)| > 0.1 in at most 7.7% of rows. Writes at the connector locus are an order of
1037
       magnitude smaller than those at the primary locus (median |𝑊𝑞,𝑞 | 0.009 against 0.044 on NIH and
1038
       0.008 against 0.238 on COCO).
1039
