1431   intervention cohort. The semantic family contains all five non-target normals from the pre-existing
1432   Qwen direction bundle (Atelectasis, Pneumothorax, Cardiomegaly, Mass, and Nodule), rather than
1433   directions chosen from the supplement outcome. Each uses the same training rows, projection, scaling,
1434
       classifier, lifting rule, and normalization as Effusion. Together with a common baseline, 20 random
       directions, and the sham, the grid produces 28 configurations and 11,200 per-image outcomes; exact
1435
       row selection appears in Appendix C.
1436
1437   Semantic ownership is a contrast on a direction–question response surface, not a property of a
1438   direction in isolation. Let 𝑊𝑞,𝑑 denote the paired mean change in question 𝑞’s yes probability after
1439   intervening with direction 𝑑 at the locked dose. A large 𝑊𝑞,𝑑 establishes that 𝑑 can write 𝑞’s answer;
1440
       it does not establish that 𝑑 owns that answer. Within a fixed clinical family, the ownership contrast is
1441                                              𝑂 𝑞 = 𝑊𝑞,𝑞 − max 𝑊𝑞,𝑑 .                                                     (8)
                                                                         𝑑≠𝑞
1442
1443   The registered supplement estimates the Effusion row of this surface, so the reported ownership
1444   contrast 𝑂 Effusion is Effusion minus its maximum alternative. The maximum is recomputed inside each
1445   of 5,000 patient-bootstrap draws. Thus 𝑂 Effusion > 0 means Effusion beats every member of the fixed
1446   clinical family, while 𝑂 Effusion < 0 means at least one alternative is stronger. Adding competitors can
1447
       only maintain or decrease 𝑂 𝑞 : a positive advantage is conditional on the candidate family, whereas a
       negative counterexample does not require an exhaustive family. This operational ownership criterion
1448
       measures relative advantage, not a necessary condition for a concept to participate in computation.
1449
       Direction specificity requires a positive Effusion effect above random p95 and absolute sham, together
1450   with a one-sided 95% lower bound for 𝑂 Effusion above zero.
1451
1452   Causal-ownership matrix. To test whether another clinical normal better matches the answer path-
1453   way, we prospectively cross six Qwen directions (Effusion, Atelectasis, Pneumothorax, Cardiomegaly,
1454   Mass, and Nodule) with their six matching questions on 400 new patients. Every question uses the
1455   same 𝛼 = +0.25, 119 random directions, and a sham. For question 𝑞, ownership requires the diagonal
1456   effect 𝑊𝑞,𝑞 to exceed every other clinical direction, every random direction, and the absolute sham
1457   effect. A centered studentized max-𝑇 bootstrap gives simultaneous 95% lower bounds over all 30
       clinical contrasts. The shared-alias family contains two statistics per direction: mean excess over


