       Under review as a conference paper at ICLR 2027




1782
       For the ownership matrix, we resample 400 patients with replacement using seed 20260904. Each
1783   draw uses the same patient indices for every question and intervention, preserving all paired baseline
1784   differences. The clinical family comprises the 30 fixed contrasts 𝑊𝑞,𝑞 − 𝑊𝑞,𝑑 for the six questions
1785   and their five alternatives. Each question’s simultaneous ownership lower bound is the minimum
1786   of its five contrast bounds. Simultaneous upper bounds use the same critical value with the sign of
1787   every contrast reversed. A question has a stronger competitor if any upper bound is below zero. A
1788   question is unresolved if it has neither a positive minimum lower bound nor a negative upper bound.
1789   The shared-alias calculation uses a separate 12-statistic family: for each of six directions, its mean
1790   off-diagonal effect and its mean excess over the five corresponding matched-direction effects. The
1791
       Mass confirmation applies the same construction to 200 independently selected patients, with seed
       20260910 and a separate family of 20 Mass-minus-alternative contrasts across four coded prompt
1792
       conditions.
1793
1794   Direct target-minus-maximum intervals summarise a different bootstrap quantity. For each draw,
1795   we recompute the largest competing mean and subtract it from the target mean. The displayed
1796   two-sided percentile intervals use the 2.5th and 97.5th percentiles of these margins. The earlier
1797
       Effusion specificity supplement uses their 5th percentile as its one-sided lower bound. These intervals
       are distinct from the simultaneous bounds on the fixed linear contrasts in Equation 9.
1798
1799   The campaign applies the same construction to every block, using 600 test rows and 2,000 shared
1800   bootstrap draws of rows (seed 2026090601). The 30 contrasts 𝑊𝑞,𝑞 − 𝑊𝑞,𝑑 receive simultaneous
1801   95% bounds from the centred studentised max-𝑇 bootstrap. 𝑂 𝑞 receives a direct percentile interval
1802   with the maximum recomputed in every draw. The logit-scale check in Table 13 applies the same
1803
       rules to margin-scale deltas.
